   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "IORQ is used in conjunction with B/A, C/D, CE and RD to transfer commands and data between the CPU and the Z80SIO.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "7837-7839",
       "sha": "11a5f56befec9b06f668a7e7820ed11e47cba72aa37b814824c8a484cbde2fe6"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "When CE, RD and IORQ are all active, the channel selected by B/A transfers data to the CPU, a read operation.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "7838-7840",
       "sha": "e63c1a8da61ae4f2bfc91de22813093727c2e639c81f4f4cdc302fb89370c2c6"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "place",
     "of": "mame",
     "text": "In ba_cd_r, offset bit 1 is B/A and offset bit 0 is C/D, the reverse of cd_ba_r, and the call goes to the selected channel's control or data read.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "898-899",
       "sha": "56d91e526928f1a713263c388af580f88b8e89ec898e4f7d0cfe467809e0cc1e"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
